 Ill, USA</conf-loc></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pan</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Pelizzari</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Image reconstruction with a shift-variant filtration in circular cone-beam CT</article-title><source><italic>International Journal of Imaging Systems and Technology</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>14</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>221</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Koizumi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kudo</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>FBP-type cone-beam reconstruction algorithm withRadon space interpolationcapabilities for axially truncated data from a circular orbit</article-title><source><italic>Medical Imaging Techonology</italic></source><year>2006</year><volume>24</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>201</fpage><lpage>208</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parker</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimal short scan convolution reconstruction for fanbeam CT</article-title><source><italic>Medical Physics</italic></source><year>1982</year><volume>9</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>254</fpage><lpage>257</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7087912</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Natterer</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><source><italic>The Mathematics of Computerized Tomography</italic></source><year>1986</year><publisher-loc>New York, NY, USA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Wiley-Teubner</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Noo</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Clackdoyle</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Pack</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A two-step Hilbert transform method for 2D image reconstruction</article-title><source><italic>Physics in Medicine and Biology</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>49</volume><issue>17</issue><fpage>3903</fpage><lpage>3923</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15470913</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kak</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Slaney</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source><italic>Principles of Computerized Tomography Imaging</italic></source><year>1987</year><publisher-loc>Piscataway, NJ, USA</publisher-loc><publisher-name>IEEE Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Starman</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fahrig</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The relationship between the T-FDK algorithm and the Hu-FDK algorithm</article-title><conf-name>In: Proceedings of  the 9th International Meeting on Fully Three-Dimensional Image Reconstruction in Radiology and Nuclear Medicine</conf-name><conf-date>July 2007</conf-date><conf-loc>Lindau, Germany</conf-loc><fpage>366</fpage><lpage>369</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>CB data acquisition geometryand coordinate system.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.001"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Illustration of thegeometry of Grangeat's formula.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Data supports in the Radon domain.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.003"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Illustration of the concept of implicit datainterpolation/extrapolation. Data point <italic>C</italic> on the approximated plane is a weightedsummation of measured data points <italic>A</italic> and <italic>B</italic>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.004"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>A vertical plane in the Radon domain.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.005"/></fig><fig id="fig6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Reconstructions of the Shepp-Logan phantom. Top row: <italic>x</italic>-<italic>z</italic> views; bottom row: <italic>y</italic>-<italic>z</italic> views. Display window: [0.98  1.05].</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.006"/></fig><fig id="fig7" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Images of the second term (Hu's term) and the thirdterm (the proposed correction term) of (<xref ref-type="disp-formula" rid="eq26">24</xref>), using the projection data on theShepp-Logan phantom. Top row: <italic>x</italic>-<italic>z</italic> views; bottom row: <italic>y</italic>-<italic>z</italic> views. Display window: [0  0.08].</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.007"/></fig><fig id="fig8" position="float"><label>Figure 8</label><caption><p>1Dcentral vertical profile comparison of <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig6">Figure 6</xref>. (a) The reduction of the axialintensity drop. (b) The reconstructed object edge using differentalgorithms.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.008"/></fig><fig id="fig9" position="float"><label>Figure 9</label><caption><p>Reconstructions of the FORBILD head phantom. Top row: <italic>x</italic>-<italic>z</italic> views; bottom row: <italic>y</italic>-<italic>z</italic> views. Display window: [1.02  1.08].</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.009"/></fig><fig id="fig10" position="float"><label>Figure 10</label><caption><p>Reconstructions of the Defrise phantom, <italic>x</italic>-<italic>z</italic> views. Display window: [0.7  1.1].</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.010"/></fig><fig id="fig11" position="float"><label>Figure 11</label><caption><p>1D central vertical profile comparison of<xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig10">Figure 10</xref>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.011"/></fig><fig id="fig12" position="float"><label>Figure 12</label><caption><p>Reconstructions of the Shepp-Logan phantom, usingnoisy projection data, <italic>x</italic>-<italic>z</italic> views. Display window: [0.98  1.05]. Based onthe noise-free reconstructions as shown in <xref ref-type="fig" rid="fig6">Figure 6</xref>, from left to right, thenoise variances in the images are measured as 5.872 &#x000d7; 10<sup>&#x02212;5</sup>, 5.872 &#x000d7; 10<sup>&#x02212;5</sup>,and 5.874 &#x000d7; 10<sup>&#x02212;5</sup>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJBI2008-242841.012"/></fig><table-wrap id="tab1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Variable glossary.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>D</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Distance from the X-ray source to the rotation center</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>D</italic><sub><italic>o</italic><italic>d</italic></sub></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Distance from the rotation center to the detector</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>f</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Scanned object</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><inline-formula><mml:math id="M68"><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mover accent="true"><mml:mi>f</mml:mi><mml:mo>^</mml:mo></mml:mover><mml:mi>c</mml:mi></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Estimation of <inline-formula><mml:math id="M69"><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mover accent="true"><mml:mi>f</mml:mi><mml:mo>^</mml:mo></mml:mover><mml:mi>N</mml:mi></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><inline-formula><mml:math id="M70"><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mrow><mml:mover accent="true"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>f</mml:mi></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mo>^</mml:mo></mml:mrow></mml:mover></mml:mrow><mml:mrow><mml:mtext>FDK</mml:mtext></mml:mrow></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Reconstruction using the FDK algorithm</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><inline-formula><mml:math id="M71"><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mover accent="true"><mml:mi>f</mml:mi><mml:mo>^</mml:mo></mml:mover><mml:mi>H</mml:mi></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Correction term in the Hu-FDK algorithm</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><inline-formula><mml:math id="M72"><mml:mrow><mml:msub><mml:mover accent="true"><mml:mi>f</mml:mi><mml:mo>^</mml:mo></mml:mover><mml:mi>N</mml:mi></mml:msub></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Missing information in the circular CB trajectory</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>g</italic><sub>0</sub></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Ramp filtering kernel</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan